t_activity_age_s": null, "list_has_generated": null, "main_agent_searched": false, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "model_context_window": 1000000, "model_max_tokens": 128000, "output_tail": "`repr()` would break for `Decimal` inputs (`\"Decimal('1.5')\"`); `str()` gives the same shortest form for floats and also works for `int`/`Decimal`.\nAdd a regression test (the task name hints at regression coverage):\n`round_money(2.675)` now returns `2.68`.\n\n**Cause:** the float `2.675` is actually stored as `2.67499999\u2026`, so `round(x, 2)` rounds it down. On top of that, `round()` rounds exact halves to the nearest even digit rather than always up, which contradicts the docstring's \"half up\".\n\n**Fix** (`pricing/money.py`): the function now converts `str(x)`, the decimal the caller wrote, to `Decimal` and rounds it with `ROUND_HALF_UP`. It still returns a `float`, so `add_vat` and other callers don't change. Using `str()` instead of `repr()` also keeps `Decimal` inputs working.\n\n**Checked:** `2.675\u21922.68`, `1.005\u21921.01`, `0.125\u21920.13`, `2.665\u21922.67`, `-2.675\u2192-2.68` (halves round away from zero), `1.234\u21921.23`, `3\u21923.0`, `add_vat(10)\u219212.0`.\n\nI added a regression test in `tests/test_round_money.py`. pytest isn't installed here, so I called the test functions directly with `python3`; they pass, and so does the existing `test_split`.\n\nNot changed: `add_vat` multiplies floats before rounding, so a product that lands just off a half (e.g. `\u20264999999`) will be rounded as that float. Fixing that would mean moving the pricing math to `Decimal`, which is a bigger change than this bug needs.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 2, "replies_ok": 11, "replies_throttled": 0, "requests_cache_read": 305416, "requests_cache_write": 14180, "requests_cost_usd": 0.18487920000000002, "requests_count": 11, "requests_input_uncached": 24, "requests_output": 2640, "reread": false, "rule_order": "none", "rule_prefix": "neit